      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Black Sunday** (1977) marked a pivotal moment in terrorism-themed thrillers, arriving years before they became a Hollywood staple. John Frankenheimer directs this taut adaptation of Thomas Harris's novel (pre-dating his Hannibal Lecter series) about a plot to detonate a bomb at the Super Bowl. The film's lasting influence shows in later sports-terrorism narratives like <a href=\"/movie/6883\" class=\"movie-title\">Two-Minute Warning</a> (1976) and **Sudden Death** (1995). Robert Shaw delivers a commanding performance as an Israeli Mossad agent, coming fresh off his iconic role in **Jaws** (1975)."
      },
