      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Frankenheimer's direction in Black Sunday reflects his masterful handling of political thrillers, building on his earlier classics like **The Manchurian Candidate** (1962) and **Seven Days in May** (1964). The film's use of actual Super Bowl X footage and a real Goodyear blimp lends unprecedented authenticity, while Bruce Dern's unhinged performance as the traumatized Vietnam vet turned terrorist pilot set new standards for complex antagonists."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's technical achievements were groundbreaking for 1977. Cinematographer John A. Alonzo, fresh from **Chinatown** (1974), captured stunning aerial sequences that influenced later action films like **Blue Thunder** (1983) and **Die Hard 2** (1990). The combination of practical effects and real football crowd footage created a sense of scale rarely achieved before CGI. SUBHEAD: Impact on Political Thrillers"
      },
