      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Black Sunday's influence extends beyond its technical innovations. Its exploration of Middle Eastern terrorism predated similar themes in films like **Delta Force** (1986) and **True Lies** (1994). The film's careful handling of complex political issues, particularly its nuanced portrayal of both Israeli and Palestinian perspectives, was ahead of its time and influenced later terrorism thrillers like **Munich** (2005)."
